# ALIVE-receipt-crown DRIVER gate (ADR-0010 re-bird), the positive image of
# the law "ALIVE requires exact candidate/subject SHA and a durable receipt"
# (mirrors shapes/work-order.shacl.ttl). The offender form — an ALIVE order
# missing sj:candidateSha / sj:subjectSha / sj:receipt — is the inverted
# companion verify/046_alive_receipt_crown.unbound.rq (zero-rows-pass,
# offender-reporting per ADR-0010:
# docs/architecture/adr/0010-gate-convention-directory-is-convention.md),
# verbatim former gates/046. The driver witnesses the crown vocabulary
# surface the law is written against: the three crown predicates are declared
# rdf:Property individuals in the pack ontology, so on the canonical graph
# this gate has one row per crown predicate (>= 1 row = the vocabulary the
# SHAPE binds is present; 0 rows = a crown predicate was dropped from the
# ontology and the ALIVE law is unwritable).
PREFIX sj: <https://ggen-igniter.dev/ontology/semantic-jira#>
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
SELECT ?property WHERE {
  {
    sj:candidateSha a rdf:Property .
    BIND(sj:candidateSha AS ?property)
  } UNION {
    sj:subjectSha a rdf:Property .
    BIND(sj:subjectSha AS ?property)
  } UNION {
    sj:receipt a rdf:Property .
    BIND(sj:receipt AS ?property)
  }
}
